<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Purple exhaust flame for the Breach Jump under Vanilla Gravship Expanded, where the tank
    burns astrofuel (VGE's astrofire and astrofuel art are purple). Mirrors VFEP's
    VFEP_JumpFlame (Royalty's JumpFlame re-exported: TransparentPostLight, solid 0.2 s, fade
    0.05 s, shrinking at -4) on VGE's own Effects/Astrospark texture, referenced by path so
    nothing is shipped or derived; this root only loads when VGE, and so that file, is present.
    Tint cannot do this on the orange texture (both mote shaders multiply, and orange has no
    blue to keep), hence the texture swap.

    Astrospark is a 128 px sheet whose opaque blob fills about a third of it (VFEP's fills
    its 64 px), so drawSize 3 brings it to the same on-screen size at the effecters' VFEP
    sprayer scales. The blob is hard-edged and irregular; the sprayer's default 0-360 random
    rotation varies it per fleck. Not yet seen in game (2026-09-18): drawSize and the tints
    in SCWC_AstroflameGlow are the knobs. Core's grey Things/Mote/BlastExtinguisher (the
    orange BlastFlame's mask with the colour removed, tintable through color) is the reserve
    route if this reads too much like a sticker.

    Also the parent of SCWC_AstroflameNorth (AstroflameNorth.xml), which inherits everything
    here and only moves the altitude up to PawnState for when the wearer faces north.
  -->
  <FleckDef Name="SCWC_Astroflame" ParentName="FleckBase_Thrown">
    <defName>SCWC_Astroflame</defName>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Effects/Astrospark</texPath>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
      <renderInstanced>true</renderInstanced>
      <drawSize>(3, 3)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>Projectile</altitudeLayer>
    <solidTime>0.2</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>0.05</fadeOutTime>
    <growthRate>-4</growthRate>
  </FleckDef>
</Defs>
